-- title:
--   Projective normality of the |(2g+1)∞| model of X₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and a natural number $k$ with $k \geq 2$. Work in the field $F =$ [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldBar N`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L111), the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $N$ inside Laurent series, regarded as an extension of $K = \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $E =$ [`ModularCurve.embDivisor N`](def/ModularCurve_JZeroHeightForm.html#L106) be the divisor $(2g+1)\cdot\bar\infty$, where $g =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.genusFF`](def/AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions.html#L145) $(\overline{\mathbb Q}, F)$ and $\bar\infty =$ [`ModularCurve.cuspInftyBar N`](def/ModularCurve_AtkinLehner.html#L93) is the distinguished place at the cusp; concretely $E$ is the finitely supported function sending $\bar\infty$ to $2g+1$ and every other place to $0$. For a divisor $D$, [`AlgebraicCurve.riemannRochSpace D`](def/AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions.html#L105) is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-submodule of $F$ consisting of those $f$ with $v(f) \leq \exp(D\,v)$ for every place $v$, the valuation being the adic valuation of $v$ in $\mathbb Z^{m0}$. The assertion is the equality of submodules $L(E) \cdot L(kE) = L((k+1)E)$, where the left-hand side is the submodule generated by all products of an element of $L(E)$ with an element of $L(kE)$, and $kE$, $(k+1)E$ denote the integer multiples of $E$.
--
--   This is the projective normality, in degrees at least $2$, of the embedding of the modular curve given by the complete linear system of $E = (2g+1)\bar\infty$, in the form of a Castelnuovo-type surjectivity of multiplication of Riemann–Roch spaces. It supplies the surjectivity needed to produce homogeneous forms realising prescribed functions on the model, and is used in the construction of the height pairing and the evaluation arguments on $J_0(N)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZero_riemannRochSpace_embDivisor_mul_eq.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_JZeroHeightForm

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000 in

theorem ModularCurve.JZero.riemannRochSpace_embDivisor_mul_eq (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (k : ℕ) (hk : 2 ≤ k) :
    AlgebraicCurve.riemannRochSpace (ModularCurve.embDivisor N)
        * AlgebraicCurve.riemannRochSpace ((k : ℤ) • ModularCurve.embDivisor N)
      = AlgebraicCurve.riemannRochSpace ((k + 1 : ℤ) • ModularCurve.embDivisor N) := by sorry
